Z||000000||87ECO5||05-29-2001||12:48 PM||||I've got aluminum rims on my Nissan Pathfinder that were painted a silver color at the factory.<P>After 100,000 miles of use, the paint on the rims themselves is still in pretty decent shape but the paint on the center caps is beginning to flake off.<P>I went to the local Pep Boys store and found something called "Silver Wheel Paint."  It's supposed to be an exact match for factory-painted silver wheels.  My guess is it's supposed to match the paint on silver hubcaps, because I painted my center caps with it and it turned out too dark.<P>Anyone have any suggestions?  I priced a new set of center caps but they're about $200 from the dealer!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">   Don't want to spend that kind of money on this thing ...<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-29-2001||09:24 PM||||Scott--They make chrome paint that doesn't look anything like chrome, but might be just what you're looking for.  Any Autozone or hardware store ought to carry it.  At about $4 a can, you might want to give it a shot (so to speak).||||reg||1
